What Is the Photoresists Market?
Photoresists are light-sensitive chemical formulations used to transfer circuit patterns onto semiconductor wafers and other substrates through photolithography. When exposed to specific wavelengths of light, these materials undergo chemical changes that allow selected portions to be removed during development, creating precise patterns for subsequent manufacturing processes.

Photoresists are essential in semiconductor wafer fabrication, advanced packaging, display panel production, and printed circuit board manufacturing. Product formulations vary according to exposure technology, resolution requirements, process compatibility, and material purity.

